        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(claude): show Max usage multiplier (5x/20x) in plan label",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Surface the Claude Max usage multiplier in the plan label — `default_claude_max_5x` / `default_claude_max_20x` now read **\"Claude Max 5x\" / \"Claude Max 20x\"** instead of a flattened \"Max\".\n- Append the multiplier only when the rate-limit tier string names the resolved plan, so a mismatched subscription type never inherits a stray multiplier.\n- Leave Pro / Team / Enterprise labels unchanged; mirrors the existing Codex Pro 5x/20x treatment (#882).\n- Update the `docs/claude.md` plan-inference note and add a CHANGELOG entry.\n\n## Root cause\n\nAnthropic encodes the Max tier in the rate-limit tier string (`default_claude_max_5x`, `default_claude_max_20x`), but `ClaudePlan.fromRateLimitTier` matched on `.contains(\"max\")` and discarded the rest, so every Max subscription rendered as a flat \"Max\". A new `usageMultiplier(for:rateLimitTier:)` extracts a `[0-9]+x` suffix and `brandedLoginMethod(rateLimitTier:)` appends it, wired through the OAuth and web label entry points.\n\nTier strings: every value this change keys on already appears in the repo's own fixtures — `default_claude_max_20x`, `claude_pro`, `claude_team`, `claude_enterprise`, `claude_max` across `ClaudeUsageTests` / `ClaudePlanResolverTests` / `ClaudeOAuthTests`; `default_claude_max_5x` I also confirmed live on a real account. Those fixtures already mix `default_claude_*` and short `claude_*` forms, so extraction is substring-based and tier-agnostic — it stays correct across that prefix variance, and a future `default_claude_team_5x` would render \"Claude Team 5x\" automatically.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `swift test --filter ClaudePlanResolverTests` — 7 tests passed (5x/20x, bare Max, mismatched team + max_5x, web path).\n- `swift test --filter ClaudeUsageTests` — 39 tests passed.\n- `make check` — SwiftFormat, SwiftLint, repository checks passed (0 violations).\n- `make test` — full 48-shard local suite passed.\n\n## Risk\n\nLow and contained to the Claude plan label string. The multiplier is appended only when the tier names the resolved plan, so Pro/Team/Enterprise output is unchanged and a mismatched subscription type cannot leak a \"5x\"/\"20x\". Downstream consumers that re-parse the label (`fromCompatibilityLoginMethod`) still resolve \"Claude Max 5x\" to `.max`, so history bucketing and subscription detection are unaffected.\n",
        "branch": "feat/claude-plan-tier-labels",
